            "question": "How does the new alerting approach group model-serving requests by the stages they pass through to reduce noisy alerts and speed up root cause analysis?",
            "reference_answer": "It adds a lightweight token_stage_cohort service that computes a deterministic \"cohort key\" for each invocation from stage-level signals (e.g., token counts per stage, KV-cache hit patterns, decode batch size) and keeps short-lived aggregates per cohort. An alert route-matrix generator then uses those cohort rollups to build a route × stage alert matrix that attributes SLO violations to the most likely pipeline stages and biases escalation to the top-k responsible stages, reducing per-route alert noise and speeding RCA.",
